+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Depth Loss:** MIP discards all depth information; a high-intensity structure in the background can occlude a closer, lower-intensity structure [S8, S12, S27, unofficial][S28][S30, S38, unofficial].
+*   **Order Independence:** The result does not depend on the order of sample processing, allowing for random access and acceleration structures [S2, unofficial][S29, book][S37, unofficial].
+*   **Hardware Blending:** Standard OpenGL blending cannot compute a maximum; the `EXT_blend_minmax` extension (`glBlendEquationEXT(GL_MAX_EXT)`) is required if using hardware blending for MIP [S9, unofficial][S36].
+*   **Degenerate Rays:** If the ray does not intersect the volume or the intersection is degenerate ($t_{near} \ge t_{far}$), the algorithm should output a background color immediately [S15, unofficial].
+*   **Precision:** When using integer or fixed-point formats for volume data, ensure the accumulator uses a type capable of holding the maximum value without overflow [S23, unofficial].
 
 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Local Maximum Intensity Projection](6054-local-maximum-intensity-projection.md)
-Selects the first local intensity maximum above a threshold instead of the global maximum, preserving some depth information.
+Selects the first local intensity maximum above a threshold instead of the global maximum, preserving some depth information and acting as an acceleration technique by discarding subsequent samples.
 
 ### [Fast Maximum Intensity Projection (MIP)](6635-fast-maximum-intensity-projection-mip.md)
-Accelerates MIP using shear-warp projection and interval decomposition to avoid unnecessary resampling.
+Accelerates MIP by decomposing the density domain into intervals and using shear-warp projection to resample only at voxel locations within the relevant interval.
 
 ### [MIP with Offset Lookup](6637-mip-with-offset-lookup.md)
-Uses binary volume masks and lookup tables to skip low-density intervals, focusing only on the highest density interval.
+Uses a binary volume mask and bitwise operations to determine the highest density interval along a ray, skipping low-density samples entirely.
 
 ### [Priority Queue MIP with Min/Max Grids](10338-priority-queue-mip-with-min-max-grids.md)
-Uses a priority queue and multilevel grids to efficiently find the maximum value, skipping regions with lower maximums.
+Combines a hierarchical min/max grid with a priority queue to skip empty or low-intensity regions during traversal.
 
 ### Morphological Maximum Intensity Projection (MMIP) with Morphological Closing
-Prevents hole formation in non-axial views caused by undersampling by applying a morphological closing operation to the 2D projection image after voxel projection [S42]. Uses a 2x2x2 structuring element [S42]. Standard MIP for axial views can overwrite old values by projecting low-to-high, but non-axial views require this closing to handle undersampling holes [S42].
